<Base
  title="Rock Your Baby — Gonzalo Ferrero Martín"
  description="A four-board baby-monitoring cradle on PYNQ-Z2s: heartbeat, crying, decision-making and actuator subsystems talking over UART, in C."
  kind="work-case"
  depth={1}
  ground="walnut"
>
<main id="main">

  <section class="page cs">
    <p class="kicker col-head"><span class="nc">TU/e</span> 5EWC0 · first year · <span class="nb">2025 – 26</span></p>
    <h1 class="col-head">Rock Your Baby</h1>
    <p class="deck col-prose">A baby-monitoring cradle split across four boards that talk over UART.</p>
    <figure class="fig fig--bleed" id="fig-1">
      <div class="fig__scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-labelledby="fig-1-cap">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 800 260" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin meet" role="img" aria-labelledby="f1t">
          <title id="f1t">Four subsystems, each on its own PYNQ-Z2: heartbeat and crying feed decision-making over UART, and decision-making commands the actuator over UART; the actuator drives two PWM channels, one for frequency and one for amplitude.</title>
          <defs>
            <marker id="arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="10" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"/></marker>
          </defs>
          <!-- heartbeat: box (0,20) 230 × 40 -->
          <rect class="crisp" x="0" y="20" width="230" height="40"/>
          <text class="t-ink" x="12" y="45">heartbeat</text>
          <text x="0" y="80">ADC → filter → BPM</text>
          <text x="0" y="98">waveform on 240×240 TFT</text>
          <text x="0" y="118">PYNQ-Z2</text>
